Not to sidetrack what I hope to accomplish in C in Nethack, but in my
day job as a Fortune 500 software architect on a modern JVM I can
achieve between 80% and 110% processing speed compared to good C++ code
for almost everything.  Runtime Hotspot optimization can do some
amazing things especially now with Java 6.  Assembly or C will almost
always be faster in the end, and C++ is often faster, but you'd be
surprised how close it generally is.

That being said, I have fiddled in the J2ME space and the various JVMs
from the different vendors have lots of quirks.  I hope with the
